SEVERITY:CRITICAL

Update CompileTest for new validation behavior.

## File to modify
itr-compiler/src/test/scala/itrcompiler/application/services/CompileTest.scala

## Required changes

### 1. Update fixture mock
The fixture (lines 9-37) returns batches that include VerificationCU and E2eVerificationCU. Since these are no longer required, the fixture can be simplified. But to maintain backward compatibility, keep them and just update assertions.

### 2. Update test "should compile a JSON batch with required parts" (line 58)
The test currently expects 5 CUs including verification and e2everification. This should still work since having extra CUs is fine. No change needed.

### 3. Update test "should throw when batch is missing required parts" (line 116)
The test expects an IllegalStateException when only a regular CU is in the batch. This should still work since ARCH and LEGEND are still required. No change needed.

### 4. Add new test: incremental compilation
it should "allow compilation when ARCH exists on disk but not in batch" in {
  val tmpDir = java.nio.file.Files.createTempDirectory("compile-test-")
  java.nio.file.Files.write(tmpDir.resolve("ARCH.itr"), "# ARCH".getBytes)
  java.nio.file.Files.write(tmpDir.resolve("LEGEND.itr"), "# LEGEND".getBytes)

  val contentRead = new ContentRead {
    def readJson(path: java.nio.file.Path) = CUBatch(Seq(
      CU(id = "cu-001", dtrCoordinates = Seq.empty, content = "content 1")
    ))
    def readYaml(path: java.nio.file.Path) = CUBatch(Seq.empty)
  }
  val compile = new Compile(
    new DTRLoad { def load(path: java.nio.file.Path): String = "" },
    new CoordinateRules,
    new CUStore(new CUWrite { def write(cu: CU, outFolder: java.nio.file.Path, force: Boolean): Unit = () }),
    new ContentDeserialize(contentRead),
    new RequiredPartsValidation
  )
  val cmd = CompileCommand(
    compile = true, dtr = None, outFolder = tmpDir.resolve("out"),
    rawContent = None, cuId = None,
    jsonContent = Some(Paths.get("batch.json")), yamlContent = None, force = false
  )
  // Should NOT throw because ARCH and LEGEND exist on disk
  // Note: outFolder is tmpDir.resolve("out") but ARCH/LEGEND are in tmpDir
  // The disk check should look in the outFolder, so this might fail
  // Adjust the test to put files in the outFolder
}

### 5. Update error message assertion
If any test asserts the exact error message string, update it to match the new message: "ITR must contain ARCH and LEGEND."

## Verification
sbt test -- -z CompileTest
